<header><p class="st-kicker">other · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Spanish Netherlands</h1><p class="st-meta">1556 CE – 1714 CE · capital Brussels</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The southern Low Countries under the Spanish Habsburgs, battleground of Europe and home of Rubens, which survived the Dutch Revolt but lost land to France.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1555–1556 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> passed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/habsburg-netherlands">Habsburg Netherlands</a> to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a>. Philip's persecution of Protestants, new bishoprics and taxes provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a> from 1566. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-alvarez-de-toledo-3rd-duke-of-alba">Duke of Alba's</a> harsh rule, the southern provinces made peace with Philip through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-arras">Union of Arras</a> in 1579.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Duke of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Parma</a> reconquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-flanders">Flanders</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-brabant">Brabant</a>, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a> in 1585, while the north became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-vii-archduke-of-austria">Archdukes Albert</a> and Isabella governed from 1598 to 1621 and agreed the Twelve Years' Truce. The provinces became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Counter-Reformation</a> stronghold; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-paul-rubens">Rubens</a> worked in Antwerp. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-munster">Treaty of Münster</a> of 1648 closed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a>, hurting Antwerp's trade.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-artois">Artois</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lille">Lille</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-cambrai">Cambrai</a> and other lands between 1659 and 1678. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-utrecht">Treaties of Utrecht</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-rastatt">Rastatt</a> in 1713–1714 gave the territory to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/austrian-netherlands">Austrian Netherlands</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/spanish-netherlands.jpg" alt="Spanish Netherlands" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Ningyou. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cross_of_Burgundy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1556 CE – 1714 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Brussels</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Philip II of Spain, Albert VII of Austria, Isabella Clara Eugenia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch and French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>, <a href="/countries/luxembourg">Luxembourg</a>, <a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Southern Netherlands (Spanish), Catholic Netherlands</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1635&amp;focus=spanish-netherlands" aria-label="Spanish Netherlands on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4779 414 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Spanish Netherlands lay"><image href="/maps/world